o cover:  \n- (0,2): I give you a B  \n- (0,3): I give you a B  \n- (1,3): I give you a B  \nYou offer to cover **any 3 R tiles of my choosing** on my route.\n\nOn my preferred (shortest B-heavy) path, my R needs are:  \n- (1,0): R (need covered)  \n- (2,3): R (need covered)  \n\nSo for **my goal.**  \nIf you cover:  \n- (1,0): You give me an R  \n- (2,3): You give me an R  \n\nYour original proposal allows up to 3 Rs, which is enough to fully cover my missing reds for this route. (Third R coverage unused by me.)\n\n**Summary of contract:**\n\nYou cover for me:  \n- (1,0): You give me an R  \n- (2,3): You give me an R  \n\nI cover for you:  \n- (0,2): I give you a B  \n- (0,3): I give you a B  \n- (1,3): I give you a B  \n\n**Analysis:**  \n- This contract lets me reach my goal, which I cannot do alone.  \n- I pay 3 blue chips for you, get 2 reds covered for myself.  \n- My remaining chips: Start (B: 14, G: 2, R: 0), minus 3 B (for you), minus 1 B and 1 G for my own moves (1,1) and (3,3). End: B: 10, G: 1, R: 0.  \n- Score: 20 (goal) + 11*5 = 75.\n\nIf I do NOT trade, I get 0 (cannot reach goal). With this contract, I get 75 points.\n\n**I accept your terms exactly as laid out above and require the following coverage:**\n\n- (1,0): You give me an R  \n- (2,3): You give me an R  \n- (0,2): I give you a B  \n- (0,3): I give you a B  \n- (1,3): I give you a B  \n\nagree \n, \nplayer 0: Excellent. This contract strictly benefits me: by taking the B-heavy path and having you cover (0,2), (0,3), and (1,3) with blue chips, I save 3 R chips for my final score. I have enough R for your coverage and don’t lose any possible points.\n\nTo confirm, the contract is:\n\n- (1,0): I give you an R  \n- (2,3): I give you an R  \n- (0,2): You give me a B  \n- (0,3): You give me a B  \n- (1,3): You give me a B  \n\nI accept these exact contract terms.\n\nagree \n",
